cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "model-drift: a public LLM regression tracker with a published detection floor"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
  Cite the archived release rather than the repository: a result belongs to the
  exact code that produced it, not to whatever main happens to hold later.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Erik
    family-names: Hill
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-5912-967X"
    email: erik@erikhill.dev
repository-code: "https://github.com/egnaro9/model-drift"
url: "https://erikhill.dev"
abstract: >-
  Is My Model Drifting? A public LLM regression tracker: a frozen, hash-
  fingerprinted suite run daily against 16 models across 5 labs, scoring
  accuracy, latency, verbosity, reliability and refusal rate. Deterministic
  grading, no LLM judge.
keywords:
  - model drift
  - regression detection
  - noise floor
  - LLM evaluation
  - monitoring
license: MIT
